{"id":"CVE-2014-8151","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2015-01-15T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T13:10:51.108Z","description":"The darwinssl_connect_step1 function in lib/vtls/curl_darwinssl.c in libcurl 7.31.0 through 7.39.0, when using the DarwinSSL (aka SecureTransport) back-end for TLS, does not check if a cached TLS session validated the certificate when reusing the session, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof servers via a crafted certificate.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2015/Aug/msg00001.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2015-08-13-2"},{"url":"http://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_20150108A.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://kb.juniper.net/InfoCenter/index?page=content&id=JSA10743","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://support.apple.com/kb/HT205031","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201701-47","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201701-47"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/61925","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"61925"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
